================================================================================
ANALYSIS / DECOMPOSITION
================================================================================

SURFACE DELIVERED (parity port of web/src/components/status/HealthRow.tsx)
  Native WinUI 3 shared surface `HealthRow` in TeslaSync.App.SharedSurfaces - the single-line
  at-a-glance health row: a status-tinted dot, an optional leading icon, a primary label, a
  right-aligned status-tinted summary (e.g. "12 / 12 healthy") and a trailing chevron when the row is
  actionable. It composes the atomic Components/Status/TsHealthRow primitive (the shared dot + icon +
  label + summary + chevron grid, with built-in pointer/Enter/Space activation and system focus
  visuals) and binds it to the UI-thread-free HealthRowViewModel, so the surface owns the binding, the
  activation routing and the diagnostics while the row visuals stay in the component library (the
  atomic is out of scope per the prompt). 44px minimum touch target (web min-h-[44px]).

STATES (all reproduced from the web source; the web has NO data fetch, so there is no loading / error
/ stale / offline chrome - the states are the presentational branches the web source actually has)
  status tint : healthy / degraded / unhealthy / unknown / maintenance (Core.Status.HealthStatus, 5 values)
  icon        : present (glyph supplied) / absent (web `icon && ...`)
  interaction : InternalLink (web <Link to>) / ExternalLink (web <a target=_blank>) /
                Command (web <button onClick>) / None (web <div>) - `to` wins over `onClick`
  chevron     : shown when actionable (web `to || onClick`) / hidden otherwise

FILES (4-file surface pattern + headless tests; subdirectory layout like LayoutBreadcrumbs/Toast)
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/HealthRow/HealthRow.Model.cs     (WinUI-free)
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/HealthRow/HealthRow.Source.cs    (WinUI-free)
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/HealthRow/HealthRow.ViewModel.cs (WinUI-free)
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/HealthRow/HealthRow.cs           (WinUI view; composes TsHealthRow)
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/HealthRowTests.cs           (34 headless tests)

BINDINGS
  P1/S8 state holders : HealthRowViewModel holds the HealthRowModel and reprojects on change (the web
    re-render on prop change). Link activation routes through the IHealthRowNavigator seam (production
    supplies a real navigator; NullHealthRowNavigator is the inert headless default); the command
    branch invokes the supplied handler. The view performs no navigation itself.
  P1/S9 tokens : the composed atomic tints the dot + summary from the canonical status palette
    (StatusPresentation, Core.Status); no raw hex in the surface.
  P1/S10 i18n  : the web HealthRow is anonymous - it renders NO literals of its own; label/summary are
    caller-supplied, already-localized strings. There are therefore no i18n message keys to add to the
    catalogue (documented in HealthRowRegistration); the " - " accessible-name join is punctuation.
  P1/S11 diag  : HealthRowDiagnostics emits exactly `view.opened slug=HealthRow`, once, on Loaded.
  Accessibility: the row is the focusable element with its Narrator name unified to the web link
    aria-label ("{label} - {summary}"); the atomic's pointer/Enter/Space activation + system focus
    visuals are reused; no animation, so reduce-motion-safe by construction.

PRE-EXISTING BLOCKER REPAIRED (required for ANY build/test to pass)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was committed with a merge=union multi-root
  corruption (TWO <Project> roots, MSB4025 "multiple root elements" at line 1357) -> the WHOLE solution
  build failed before any change. Consolidated into ONE canonical <Project> root and the Compile
  ItemGroup regenerated as the case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated UNION of the
  two corrupt roots (the documented recovery in the file's own INVARIANT). The two roots had diverged
  (root-1 uniquely held AnimatedMarker/RoutePlayback/RouteTransition/VehiclePicker; root-2 uniquely held
  MapTileLayer - all have tests), so the union was required to lose nothing; plus the 3 new HealthRow
  WinUI-free logic links (the HealthRow.cs view is correctly excluded). Result: 1244 Compile items,
  single root, valid XML. Same repair precedent named in the file's own header
  (VehiclePicker/SortControl/RoutePlayback/AnimatedMarker/LayoutBreadcrumbs) and the ServiceStatus gate.

